    '''
    In computing, any given ASCII string is represented with its bytes in a 
    particular numerical base. For example, a COBOL computer uses binary (base-2), 
    a mainframe computer uses hexadecimal (base-16), a smartphone computer uses decimal (base-10), 
    and a virus infected mainframe uses trinary (base-3). 
    Write a function that takes string num_as_string and two bases b1 and b2 as arguments, 
